Description: terminal tool for configuring UBX GNSS receivers (unofficial)
 ubxctl is a terminal user interface for configuring u-blox generation 9
 and later GNSS receivers over a serial or USB port. It shows the fix,
 satellites and RF status, browses and edits every configuration key in
 the RAM, BBR and Flash layers, sets message output rates, and imports,
 exports and applies presets.
 .
 ubxctl is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
 or supported by u-blox AG.
 .
 This package bundles the pyubx2, pynmeagps and pyrtcm Python libraries,
 which are not packaged in Debian.
